    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Energy Conservation [S+N]\n\nNo friction acts, so $E = T + V$ must stay at its initial value. The symbolic energy, with the numeric parameters substituted, becomes a function of the four state variables. Its relative drift over the run measures the integration error independently of the equations of motion.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "E_expr : float(subst(params, subst(equal_ml, subst(derivs, T + V))))$\nE_f : buildq([e : E_expr], lambda([theta1, theta2, w1, w2], e))$\nE_t : map(lambda([r], E_f(r[2], r[3], r[4], r[5])), rows)$\nE0 : first(E_t)$\ndrift : lmax(map(lambda([e], abs(e - E0)), E_t))/abs(E0)$\nprintf(true, \"E(0) = ~,10f J, max relative drift over 20 s: ~,2e~%\", E0, drift)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "E(0) = 16.0240198016 J, max relative drift over 20 s: 2.87e-10"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Sensitivity to Initial Conditions [N]\n\nA second run starts with $\\theta_1$ larger by $10^{-9}$ rad. The distance between the two runs in the four-dimensional phase space, $d(t) = |\\mathbf{y}_A(t) - \\mathbf{y}_B(t)|$, grows roughly as $e^{\\lambda t}$ while it is small, where $\\lambda$ is the largest Lyapunov exponent. For contrast, the same perturbation goes into a low-energy start at $\\theta_1 = \\theta_2 = 0.3$ rad, close to the linear regime.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "separation(y0) := block([a, b],\n  a : args(np_to_matrix(np_cvode(rhs_num, state, y0, t_big, 1e-12, 1e-12, adams))),\n  b : args(np_to_matrix(np_cvode(rhs_num, state, y0 + [1e-9, 0, 0, 0], t_big,\n                                 1e-12, 1e-12, adams))),\n  makelist(sqrt((a[i][2] - b[i][2])^2 + (a[i][3] - b[i][3])^2\n              + (a[i][4] - b[i][4])^2 + (a[i][5] - b[i][5])^2), i, 1, length(a)))$\nd_high : separation(y0_big)$\nd_low : separation([0.3, 0.3, 0.0, 0.0])$\ntimes : np_to_list(t_big)$\nlog10f(x) := float(log(x)/log(10))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"crimson\", line_width=1.5, name=\"θ1 = 2.0, θ2 = 2.5\",\n  lines(times, map(log10f, d_high)),\n  color=\"steelblue\", name=\"θ1 = θ2 = 0.3\",\n  lines(times, map(log10f, d_low)),\n  title=\"Separation of Two Runs Started 1e-9 rad Apart\",\n  xlabel=\"t (s)\", ylabel=\"log10 d(t)\", grid=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 12,
      "outputs": [
        {
