6,-8.643281188473805,-8.65038374233256,-8.648125451203994,-8.636615994634631,-8.617011485914581,-8.591345531680437,-8.561886865962848,-8.53046003820927,-8.49822881333893,-8.466376305248,-8.435655444161311,-8.406487006601822,-8.379019879444849,-8.353267026974956,-8.329448950368928,-8.307515261808064,-8.287451358591635,-8.269239635342567,-8.252799420878638,-8.238066877094198,-8.225025649956276,-8.21363008151801,-8.203781118253918,-8.19545908309965,-8.188627276540359,-8.18321487830459,-8.179186116495671,-8.17651277498592,-8.17514617243026,-8.175027124349505,-8.176140855585178,-8.17843786439075,-8.181928229204452,-8.186569162039307,-8.192285212347919,-8.199373250626687,-8.20772711963072,-8.216755400759018,-8.228349120927884,-8.240509769708568,-8.253642033980297,-8.267919503892347,-8.283366484161697,-8.300035702071531,-8.317966324850344,-8.337201481168385,-8.357894454721976,-8.380108470760756,-8.40377025519372,-8.42888162657762,-8.455410438728107,-8.483263823515777,-8.512256347115402,-8.542052168840778,-8.57212729411101,-8.601673415434483,-8.62952371367522,-8.654135883681128,-8.67368714664633,-8.686355841936681,-8.690782079594015,-8.686506013024351,-8.674144940220769,-8.655163799095623,-8.6313919072544,-8.60467232558523,-8.57651483478208,-8.547965863172076,-8.519917102634908,-8.492952431374311,-8.467358318630705,-8.443266026741856,-8.420879413346908,-8.400132280125103,-8.381055701722682,-8.36361171095919,-8.347760575476467,-8.33340702666281,-8.320649151612841,-8.309291229855532,-8.299396800881453,-8.290902009742933,-8.283772282706128,-8.278003776249461,-8.27357742853059,-8.27044733378982,-8.268622582174219,-8.268099731501179,-8.26888775676653,-8.271002362724747,-8.274439414121296,-8.279233212789542,-8.285407894619505,-8.293009807913183,-8.302082490767276,-8.312677198837466,-8.324854006708112],\"type\":\"scatter\",\"mode\":\"lines\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"steelblue\",\"width\":1.5},\"name\":\"θ1 = θ2 = 0.3\"}],\"layout\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"Separation of Two Runs Started 1e-9 rad Apart\"},\"showlegend\":true,\"width\":700,\"height\":450,\"plot_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"paper_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"xaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"t (s)\"},\"showgrid\":true,\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1},\"yaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"log10 d(t)\"},\"showgrid\":true,\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1}}}"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "The high-energy separation climbs nine orders of magnitude in about ten seconds and then saturates at the size of the phase space. The low-energy separation stays below $10^{-8}$ for the whole run.\n\n## Estimating the Lyapunov Exponent [N]\n\nA least-squares line through $\\ln d(t)$ over the growth phase gives $\\lambda$. The window starts where $d$ first exceeds $10^{-8}$, after the initial transient, and ends where it first exceeds $10^{-2}$, before saturation. The same fit over the whole low-energy run gives a slope near zero.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "first_above(d, level) := block([i : 1], while d[i] <= level do i : i + 1, i)$\nslope(ts, ys) := block([n : length(ts), tm, ym],\n  tm : apply(\"+\", ts)/n, ym : apply(\"+\", ys)/n,\n  apply(\"+\", (ts - tm)*(ys - ym))/apply(\"+\", (ts - tm)^2))$\n\ni0 : first_above(d_high, 1e-8)$\ni1 : first_above(d_high, 1e-2)$\nlambda_high : slope(rest(firstn(times, i1), i0 - 1), map(log, rest(firstn(d_high, i1), i0 - 1)))$\nlambda_low : slope(times, map(log, d_low))$\nprintf(true, \"growth window: t = ~,2f s to ~,2f s~%\", times[i0], times[i1])$\nprintf(true, \"high energy: lambda = ~,2f 1/s, separation e-folds every ~,2f s~%\",\n       lambda_high, 1/lambda_high)$\nprintf(true, \"low energy:  slope = ~,4f 1/s, largest separation ~,1e~%\",\n       lambda_low, lmax(d_low))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "growth window: t = 0.82 s to 8.52 s\nhigh energy: lambda = 1.82 1/s, separation e-folds every 0.55 s\nlow energy:  slope = 0.0086 1/s, largest separation 6.7e-9"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "A single pair of runs gives a finite-time estimate that varies with the window and the starting point. Averaging over many starts on the same energy surface would tighten it. The low-energy motion is quasi-periodic: the perturbation shifts the phase of the two modes slightly and the separation grows no faster than linearly.\n\n## Animation [N]\n\nThe animation replays the first 12 s of the large-amplitude run. `animate` substitutes a float value of its parameter into the object, so the frame positions come from rules that `tellsimpafter` fires only when the argument is a number: `frame_xs(t)` stays symbolic, while `frame_xs(1.5)` looks up the sample at $t = 1.5$ s.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "dt_frame : 0.05$\nn_frames : 241$\nstride : round(dt_frame/0.01)$\nxs_frames : makelist([0.0, bob1(rows[i])[1], bob2(rows[i])[1]], i, 1, 1 + stride*(n_frames - 1), stride)$\nys_frames : makelist([0.0, bob1(rows[i])[2], bob2(rows[i])[2]], i, 1, 1 + stride*(n_frames - 1), stride)$\nmatchdeclare(tt, numberp)$\ntellsimpafter(frame_xs(tt), xs_frames[round(tt/dt_frame) + 1])$\ntellsimpafter(frame_ys(tt), ys_frames[round(tt/dt_frame) + 1])$\n[frame_xs(1.5), frame_xs(tau)];",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ \\left[ 0.0 , -0.6528692437285091 , -1.4833530425992794 \\right]  , {\\it frame\\_xs}\\left(\\tau\\right) \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 14,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "trail : firstn(path2, 1 + stride*(n_frames - 1))$\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"lightgray\", line_width=1, lines(map(first, trail), map(second, trail)),\n  color=\"steelblue\", line_width=4,\n  animate(lines(frame_xs(tau), frame_ys(tau)), [tau, 0, 12, n_frames]),\n  color=\"black\", marker_size=12,\n  animate(points(frame_xs(tau), frame_ys(tau)), [tau, 0, 12, n_frames]),\n  aspect_ratio=true, xrange=[-2.2, 2.2], yrange=[-2.2, 2.2],\n  title=\"Double Pendulum, First 12 s\", xlabel=\"x (m)\", ylabel=\"y (m)\",\n  showlegend=false, slider_label=\"t (s)\", fps=20\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
